9 of 10 test weekdays exceed the twin's capacity for this movement under plan C (within: 2026-10-02; too few for a separate test). Real-timing weekday results are therefore NOT evidence about GDOT's controller; use the Saturday block for real timing. Webster gives P8 a larger share of a shorter cycle (about v/c 0.88 on the busiest day) and RL adapts, so both are mostly below capacity for this movement (on the highest-demand day some Webster/RL runs still have isolated teleports); they are compared on the same counts, so that comparison stays paired and fair.

